WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.638
Its classical engine read a quarter of the pixels and flagged 3 critical findings.

2
00:00:06.688 --> 00:00:09.241
It will not sign them off. A person must.

3
00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:16.798
Drishyam, an Agentic Vision entry to the OpenCV AI Competition, powered by AWS.

4
00:00:17.848 --> 00:00:23.423
Built by Vaibhav Jangid, lead engineer, and Bhavya Dhoot, design and presentation.

5
00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:29.932
America has about 625,000 bridges, inspected at least every two years.

6
00:00:29.982 --> 00:00:34.679
One drone inspection took more than 2,500 photos of one bridge.

7
00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:39.286
Drishyam is for the engineer reviewing them: it zooms in only where needed.

8
00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:45.541
Recorded 18 October on the classical engine; the site now runs the trained v1.

9
00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:49.648
Live on AWS: OpenCV 5 on an arm Lambda.

10
00:00:49.658 --> 00:00:53.755
Watch it inspect a bridge; a privacy pass finds nothing to blur.

11
00:00:53.765 --> 00:00:57.198
One survey look at the whole photo, at one eighth size.

12
00:00:57.208 --> 00:01:01.959
Entropy 0.69, above 0.5: unsure, so it zooms in.

13
00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:05.728
It moves to the best region and double-checks one level finer.

14
00:01:05.738 --> 00:01:11.090
The masks disagree: unconfirmed. Exposed rebar always goes to a person.

15
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:11.955
A second spall;

16
00:01:11.965 --> 00:01:17.118
then it stops, the next look not worth its cost, and misses a crack it never visited.

17
00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:21.357
Only a person can approve; then the server signs the work order.

18
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.151
Change one character of the signature: the server refuses it.

19
00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:26.863
Now, break it.

20
00:01:26.963 --> 00:01:30.607
Slow the segmenter, and the governor switches to the fast model.

21
00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:34.348
The planner drill sends a shell command; the allow-list rejects it.

22
00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:38.892
KILL halts it before the next look; Resume replays the moves and carries on.

23
00:01:38.992 --> 00:01:43.114
No language model runs live; these planners are scripted to fail.

24
00:01:43.764 --> 00:01:47.906
Over MCP, Claude drove the same tools on the same photo.

25
00:01:47.956 --> 00:01:52.496
At call 6 the rebar masks disagreed, so Claude handed it to a human.

26
00:01:52.546 --> 00:01:57.686
At call 18 they agreed on a spall; at call 20, the budget ended the search.

27
00:01:57.736 --> 00:01:59.504
It still missed the large spall.

28
00:02:00.154 --> 00:02:04.754
Each step is perception, decision and action, with a human gate at the end.

29
00:02:04.764 --> 00:02:08.808
CloudFront and a rate-limiting firewall front the arm Lambda;

30
00:02:08.818 --> 00:02:12.448
DynamoDB keeps kill flags, Secrets Manager the key.

31
00:02:12.458 --> 00:02:18.578
OpenCV does the looking: a pyramid, saliency, warpPerspective as a pan-tilt-zoom camera,

32
00:02:18.588 --> 00:02:20.709
a blur gate, face blurring.

33
00:02:20.719 --> 00:02:25.749
The site now runs v1 on OpenCV 5's new DNN engine.

34
00:02:25.759 --> 00:02:32.275
On Lambda a step took under 90 ms at p95 then, and under 1.2 s now.

35
00:02:32.925 --> 00:02:40.412
On 200 synthetic photos it finds 87 % of full tiling's recall at 26 % of the pixels,

36
00:02:40.422 --> 00:02:42.893
short of its 90 % target.

37
00:02:42.903 --> 00:02:45.330
One downscaled pass does about as well.

38
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.899
Ablations: only dropping the survey look loses recall,

39
00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:52.651
and a random gaze order matches it on smaller photos.

40
00:02:52.661 --> 00:02:57.864
On 200 real CODEBRIM photos, held out, the trained v1 finds 49 %:

41
00:02:57.874 --> 00:03:02.204
two and a half times the classical engine's 1 in 5.

42
00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.434
But its boxes find 30 % at random,

43
00:03:04.444 --> 00:03:08.554
and a person gets five and a half times the critical boxes.

44
00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:15.039
On 51 undamaged synthetic photos, the classical engine flags 2 in 3; v1, none.

45
00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:18.934
Our own wall, no ground truth: no region was proposed,

46
00:03:18.944 --> 00:03:23.172
so the trained segmenter never ran, and missed the hairline crack.

47
00:03:24.022 --> 00:03:28.339
On a second wall, one close look flagged a crack on the lower of two we traced,

48
00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:31.063
and never looked closely at most of the wall.

49
00:03:31.913 --> 00:03:33.237
Failures in the open:

50
00:03:33.247 --> 00:03:38.007
graffiti read as spalling, a formwork line as a crack, glare, and blur.

51
00:03:38.057 --> 00:03:42.122
Only the glare gate caught its case; three fixes are not built yet.

52
00:03:42.772 --> 00:03:48.640
Pixels, not millimetres. AI-assisted, not an inspection. Only a person can approve.

53
00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:53.694
make test, make eval, and one script for the AWS stack.

54
00:03:54.244 --> 00:03:57.908
Drishyam. It looks where it matters, and asks a human first.
